# Workspace Sync LLM Guide

## Purpose

Create or refresh the `.enclosure/` contract agents read before edits.

## When To Run

- Run init when `.enclosure/` is missing.
- Run update after CLI upgrades or guidance refresh.
- Run migrate to merge new config keys without overwriting local recipes or rules.

## How To Read The Result

- Created entries are new assets.
- Updated entries are packaged assets refreshed from the CLI.
- Preserved entries are local assets kept intact.
- Config warnings need review; validation errors stop writes.

## Examples

- If init creates the contract, read it before editing project code.
- After init, run `enclosure --llm`, `enclosure workspace rules route --task calibration`, and `enclosure health`.
- If update preserves local assets, treat them as user-owned knowledge.
- If update changes shared guidance, rerun relevant checks before contract-sensitive edits.

## Agent Tips

- Do not overwrite local rules just to refresh guidance.
- After sync, read the contract before editing application code.
- Confirm files read, reason, stop point, focused checks, and post-change `enclosure health`.
- Run contract checks when contract rules changed.
